WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.930
Every twenty-seven minutes, someone in Goa is bitten by a dog.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.620
In 2025 alone, that was nineteen thousand, three hundred and sixty-eight bite cases.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.480
And when you find an injured animal on the road, who do you even call?

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.440
Every municipality runs its own helpline.

5
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.440
Some close at eight in the evening.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:27.010
And last year, Canacona, Sankhalim, Valpoi and Mapusa held no sterilisation camps at all.

7
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.350
Meet PawSOS Goa: one WhatsApp number for every animal emergency in the state.

8
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.530
No app to install.

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.830
Here it is, working.

10
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:40.170
You send a photo of the animal, and your location.

11
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:48.660
Within seconds, Claude looks at the photo and replies: how urgent it seems, and two or three safe things to do while you wait.

12
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.810
It is guidance, never a diagnosis.

13
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:57.530
If someone else reports the same animal nearby, PawSOS merges it into the same case.

14
00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.900
The team gets one alert, not two.

15
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.950
The nearest partner team gets the photo, a map link, and two buttons: accept, or decline.

16
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:12.050
If nobody answers in time, the case moves on to the next team, and then to the taluka officer.

17
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.330
Nothing waits forever.

18
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.210
Accepted. On site. Resolved.

19
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:20.360
And the person who reported it hears every single step.

20
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:29.240
For officials, every case sits on one map, with a full audit trail, and a suggestion for where the next sterilisation camp is needed.

21
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.850
Under the hood, it is one Python service and one PostGIS database.

22
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.950
WhatsApp, Telegram and this web demo all arrive as the same message, so they run the same logic.

23
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.710
One state machine owns every case and records every change.

24
00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.850
If the AI is slow, the case is routed anyway.

25
00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.410
If a message fails to send, the case is never lost.

26
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:59.060
The teams in this demo are placeholders, and the WhatsApp line is waiting on Meta's business verification.

27
00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.630
But the whole loop works today.

28
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:06.420
This is PawSOS Goa. One number. Every report heard.
